#show: docs-subsubchapter.with(
  title: [$C - F$ Bond in Drug Design],
  route: "en",
)
The high electronegativity (@sec:en) of fluorine ($chi_{F} = 4.0$) compared to carbon ($chi_{C} = 2.5$) leads to a polar covalent bond in $C - F$ compounds. Thus, a molecule with such bonds would be electron poor as fluorine attracts the shared electrons more strongly. Also, oxidation (@sec:oxidation) involves losing an electron, molecules that are electron poor are harder to oxidize.

This property is significant as many metabolic enzymes requires oxidation, hence fluorination makes the drug molecule more metabolically stable.

